  accTitle: Form submission and database persistence
  accDescr: Browser validation starts a mutation. The Server Action validates the request and writes to the database. A successful result triggers targeted query invalidation in the browser, a refetch through a server endpoint and an updated cached list. Failures preserve the draft.
  subgraph B[Browser · draft]
    F[Form + Zod validation] --> M[TanStack mutation]
  end
  subgraph S[Server]
    A[Server Action validates request] --> D[(Write to database)]
  end
  subgraph R[Browser · cached data]
    Q[Invalidate task query] --> V[Refetch via server endpoint]
    V --> C[Update cached list]
  end
  M --> A
  D -->|Successful result| Q
  D -.->|Failure: keep draft| F
